 "shared_ring_elevation_note": "Identical to 1e-6 deg across all six recordings and equal to configs/sourcecraft-sensor-profile.json within rounding. Within one scan a ring varies by 3e-6 deg, so the driver applies a fixed elevation table rather than per-point angles. Whether that table is this unit factory calibration or a generic model table cannot be told from a bag.",
 "conclusion": "Six recordings are two capture configurations of the same sensor model and the same angular table: one 360 deg emission grid on /sensing/lidar/hesai128/pointcloud with frame_id lidar_livox, and five 120 deg sector recordings on /lidar_points with frame_id hesai_lidar. Mounting differs between them by about 0.41 m in height and 3.3 deg in roll, while configs/detector.json applies a single sensor_rotation and a zero translation to all six. Deskew must stay disabled: the sector recordings acquire over a third of the frame period, which the [0,1] normalisation would stretch into a full inter-frame motion increment."
}
